# Normalize line endings for every text file in the repository.
#
# Why: with core.autocrlf=true, a checkout rewrites LF into CRLF in the
# working copy. The publish script reads the working copy to build blobs, so
# the same logical file produced a different blob sha on every other run.
# That defeated the resume logic and stacked duplicate commits on main.
#
# With an explicit .gitattributes the checkout rule is the same on every
# machine, and the scripts below keep their exact bytes.
* text=auto

.gitattributes text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.java text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.pro text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.apk binary
*.wav binary
*.jar binary
*.so binary
*.zip binary
